# lidar-mcp — Cursor Rules

## Commands
```powershell
uv run python -m lidar_mcp.main          # Start server
uv run ruff check src/                   # Lint
```

## Architecture
FastMCP 3.4+ server wrapping YDLIDAR serial protocol driver.

## Code Standards
- Ruff Python linting (line length 120)
- READ_ONLY annotation on all tools
- No bare `except: pass`

## Session Context (lidar-mcp)
Before starting work: call `lidar_scan(operation="ports")` to confirm which
serial port the YDLIDAR is on (or read `LIDAR_PORT`); use
`lidar_scan(operation="scan")` for a single 360-degree sweep and
`show_lidar_health_card()` for the Prefab summary.
At end of work: run `uv run ruff check src/` and `uv run pytest tests/ -q`;
never commit a port change without updating WEBAPP_PORTS.md (SSE default 11075).
